## Supporting test (tests OBS, not AI output)

Using a Python script (`obsws-python`) I connected to OBS with authentication and tried to switch scenes:

| Input | Result |
|---|---|
| Existing scene name | Switched successfully |
| Missing scene name | Error 600, source not found |
| Empty string | Error 300, missing `sceneName` field |
| 200-character name | Error 600, source not found |

The scene list was unchanged afterward, so OBS does not auto-create scenes when asked to switch to a missing one. Grok described Cut's `applyLlmScene` as *creating* a scene before cutting, so Cut would need to do that explicitly. I have not tested that yet.

